findings.body:
The diff removes the early `if samples.is_empty() { return 0; }` guard. With an empty slice, `samples.iter().sum()` yields 0 and `samples.len() as u32` is 0, so line 4 becomes `0 / 0`, an integer division by zero that panics in both debug and release builds.

Trigger: Calling average(&[]) with an empty slice.{}

Impact: Callers that pass an empty sample set (the doc comment on line 1 promises 0 in that case) now get a panic instead of 0. Any caller on a hot path with possibly empty input can crash.
